    "bio": "a Representative from Tennessee; born in Virginia, ca. 1782; attended the common schools and graduated from the University of Tennessee at Knoxville; elected as a Jackson Republican to the Eighteenth Congress (March 4, 1823-March 3, 1825); elected as a Jacksonian candidate to the Twenty-first and to the two succeeding Congresses; reelected as an Anti-Jacksonian candidate to the Twenty-fourth Congress; and reelected as a Whig to the Twenty-fifth Congress and served from March 4, 1829, until his death near Kingston, Tenn., August 20, 1837, while on his way to Washington, D.C.; interment in the Baptist Cemetery, Kingston, Tenn.",
